.TH RASKIN 1
.SH NAME
raskin \- Read macOS preferences into KDL and generate native commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraskin\fR [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture persisted macOS preferences as editable KDL, then generate a standalone .macos file. Raskin never executes generated commands. Capture defaults to apple: macOS system categories plus Terminal. Select an individual category or use broad for the wider supported stores, including third\-party apps.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\-spec\fR
Emit the jdx/usage interface specification
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcapture\fR
Read explicit persisted user, host, system and container preferences plus native power profiles. Only settings supported by generation enter KDL; unavailable or unsupported settings are omitted and summarized on stderr. No settings are changed. With \-\-from, only the supplied offline tree is read; there is no live fallback.
.TP
\fBgenerate\fR
Validate saved KDL and emit native commands for a human to inspect and run. Generation never reads host settings or executes commands. Supported settings are generated by default; unsupported settings are skipped and summarized. Use \-\-strict to fail before output if any setting is unsupported.
.SH "RASKIN CAPTURE"
Read explicit persisted user, host, system and container preferences plus native power profiles. Only settings supported by generation enter KDL; unavailable or unsupported settings are omitted and summarized on stderr. No settings are changed. With \-\-from, only the supplied offline tree is read; there is no live fallback.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR raskin capture [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Show per\-source capture diagnostics on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Select Apple system categories plus Terminal, a category, or broad settings
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRapple
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<DIRECTORY>\fR
Read an offline tree containing user/, system/, containers/, host\-id.txt, and pmset.txt
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write KDL to this path; otherwise use stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Atomically replace an existing output file
.SH "RASKIN GENERATE"
Validate saved KDL and emit native commands for a human to inspect and run. Generation never reads host settings or executes commands. Supported settings are generated by default; unsupported settings are skipped and summarized. Use \-\-strict to fail before output if any setting is unsupported.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR raskin generate [OPTIONS] <INPUT>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Show per\-setting generation diagnostics on stderr
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the script to this path; otherwise use stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Atomically replace an existing output file
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Fail before writing if any setting is unsupported
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-unsupported\fR
Compatibility option: unsupported settings are already skipped by default
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<INPUT>\fR
KDL input path, or \- to read stdin
